1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,980
Last lesson you published a jar. A real repository wants a password.

2
00:00:05,530 --> 00:00:10,202
Where does that password go? Not in your build script. Not in a file that goes to git.

3
00:00:10,752 --> 00:00:14,400
Gradle has a clean path for settings, and another for secrets.

4
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:17,113
You will see a password leak from a file,

5
00:00:17,113 --> 00:00:17,641
remove it,

6
00:00:17,641 --> 00:00:19,857
and bring it back through the environment.

7
00:00:20,407 --> 00:00:23,521
Then you do it alone, and a checker judges your result.

8
00:00:24,071 --> 00:00:28,658
One idea first: settings go in files. Secrets go in the environment.

9
00:00:30,208 --> 00:00:33,792
Four ideas keep a Gradle build configurable, and safe.

10
00:00:34,342 --> 00:00:39,739
One, settings live in gradle dot properties. Not secret, and shared by the whole team.

11
00:00:40,289 --> 00:00:40,558
Two,

12
00:00:40,558 --> 00:00:43,710
a flag on the command line overrides a setting,

13
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:44,515
for one run.

14
00:00:44,515 --> 00:00:46,327
The flag is dash capital P.

15
00:00:46,877 --> 00:00:47,251
Three,

16
00:00:47,251 --> 00:00:50,242
a secret never goes in a file that is committed.

17
00:00:50,242 --> 00:00:52,112
It comes from the environment,

18
00:00:52,112 --> 00:00:53,234
or a secret store.

19
00:00:53,784 --> 00:00:59,245
Four, read it, but never print it. A build log is public, and a leaked line stays forever.

20
00:00:59,795 --> 00:01:02,255
Real Nexus needs a user and a password.

21
00:01:02,255 --> 00:01:04,400
This is how they reach your build.

22
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,598
Let us see it live.

23
00:01:07,648 --> 00:01:13,451
Go into the project. Type: CD, slash opt, slash lab ninety-eight, slash cartcore.

24
00:01:14,001 --> 00:01:18,353
First, look at the settings file. Type: cat, gradle dot properties.

25
00:01:20,403 --> 00:01:21,111
One line.

26
00:01:21,111 --> 00:01:22,213
Repo password,

27
00:01:22,213 --> 00:01:22,764
equals,

28
00:01:22,764 --> 00:01:23,630
Pa55-plain.

29
00:01:23,630 --> 00:01:24,890
A real password,

30
00:01:24,890 --> 00:01:26,149
in a plain file.

31
00:01:26,149 --> 00:01:27,724
If this goes to git,

32
00:01:27,724 --> 00:01:31,581
everyone who can read the repository can read it.

33
00:01:32,131 --> 00:01:33,897
What does the build see?

34
00:01:33,897 --> 00:01:35,736
Run the show config task,

35
00:01:35,736 --> 00:01:36,766
in quiet mode.

36
00:01:36,766 --> 00:01:38,606
Type: dot slash gradle W,

37
00:01:38,606 --> 00:01:39,120
dash Q,

38
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:40,003
show config.

39
00:01:42,053 --> 00:01:42,673
Greeting,

40
00:01:42,673 --> 00:01:43,087
unset.

41
00:01:43,087 --> 00:01:43,707
Password,

42
00:01:43,707 --> 00:01:43,983
set.

43
00:01:43,983 --> 00:01:46,808
The build found the password in the file.

44
00:01:46,808 --> 00:01:49,081
Notice what the task prints: set,

45
00:01:49,081 --> 00:01:50,184
never the value.

46
00:01:50,184 --> 00:01:51,700
A build log is public.

47
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:53,147
Never print a secret.

48
00:01:53,697 --> 00:01:55,795
Take the secret out of the file.

49
00:01:55,795 --> 00:01:58,221
Delete every line with repo password.

50
00:01:58,221 --> 00:01:58,877
Type: sed,

51
00:01:58,877 --> 00:01:59,336
dash I,

52
00:01:59,336 --> 00:02:00,909
then the delete command,

53
00:02:00,909 --> 00:02:02,614
and gradle dot properties.

54
00:02:04,664 --> 00:02:06,392
Ask again. Same command.

55
00:02:08,442 --> 00:02:08,970
Password,

56
00:02:08,970 --> 00:02:09,439
missing.

57
00:02:09,439 --> 00:02:11,023
The build no longer has it,

58
00:02:11,023 --> 00:02:12,079
and nothing leaks.

59
00:02:12,079 --> 00:02:13,546
Now we must give it back,

60
00:02:13,546 --> 00:02:14,309
the safe way.

61
00:02:14,859 --> 00:02:18,091
A setting that is not secret belongs in the file.

62
00:02:18,091 --> 00:02:19,081
Add a greeting.

63
00:02:19,081 --> 00:02:19,806
Type: echo,

64
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:20,664
the greeting,

65
00:02:20,664 --> 00:02:21,983
double greater than,

66
00:02:21,983 --> 00:02:23,435
gradle dot properties.

67
00:02:25,485 --> 00:02:26,487
Ask the build.

68
00:02:29,037 --> 00:02:30,976
Greeting: Welcome to CloudCart.

69
00:02:30,976 --> 00:02:32,728
The setting lives in a file,

70
00:02:32,728 --> 00:02:35,480
so everyone on the team gets the same value.

71
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:38,506
Sometimes you need a different value,

72
00:02:38,506 --> 00:02:38,840
once.

73
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:40,981
Override it on the command line,

74
00:02:40,981 --> 00:02:42,319
with dash capital P.

75
00:02:42,319 --> 00:02:43,524
Type: show config,

76
00:02:43,524 --> 00:02:44,862
then dash capital P,

77
00:02:44,862 --> 00:02:46,334
greeting equals Hello.

78
00:02:48,384 --> 00:02:53,099
Greeting: Hello. The command line wins over the file, and the file did not change.

79
00:02:53,649 --> 00:02:54,726
Now the secret,

80
00:02:54,726 --> 00:02:56,879
the safe way: the environment.

81
00:02:56,879 --> 00:02:58,531
A variable named O R G,

82
00:02:58,531 --> 00:02:59,320
underscore,

83
00:02:59,320 --> 00:02:59,823
gradle,

84
00:02:59,823 --> 00:03:00,613
underscore,

85
00:03:00,613 --> 00:03:01,187
project,

86
00:03:01,187 --> 00:03:01,977
underscore,

87
00:03:01,977 --> 00:03:03,628
then the property name.

88
00:03:03,628 --> 00:03:05,638
Set it for this one command.

89
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:08,598
Password: set.

90
00:03:08,598 --> 00:03:11,525
Gradle turned the variable into the property.

91
00:03:11,525 --> 00:03:13,866
The value came from the environment,

92
00:03:13,866 --> 00:03:15,622
so it never touched a file.

93
00:03:15,622 --> 00:03:16,533
In a pipeline,

94
00:03:16,533 --> 00:03:18,419
the secret store provides it.

95
00:03:18,969 --> 00:03:19,616
Prove it.

96
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:21,917
Search every file for the value,

97
00:03:21,917 --> 00:03:23,499
and count the matches.

98
00:03:23,499 --> 00:03:24,793
Type: grep dash R,

99
00:03:24,793 --> 00:03:25,512
the value,

100
00:03:25,512 --> 00:03:25,800
dot,

101
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,519
then pipe,

102
00:03:26,519 --> 00:03:27,310
W C dash L.

103
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:34,245
Zero. The secret was used, and left no trace in the project. That is the goal.

104
00:03:35,795 --> 00:03:39,315
Your task. The same journey, on your own project, in the lab.

105
00:03:39,865 --> 00:03:45,412
One: the password sits in gradle dot properties. Take it out. No file may contain it.

106
00:03:45,962 --> 00:03:50,207
Two: add a greeting to gradle dot properties, and see it in show config.

107
00:03:50,757 --> 00:03:53,951
Three: override the greeting with dash capital P,

108
00:03:53,951 --> 00:03:56,624
and save the output in override dot text.

109
00:03:57,174 --> 00:04:00,163
Four: give the password through the environment,

110
00:04:00,163 --> 00:04:02,593
and save the output in secret dot text.

111
00:04:02,593 --> 00:04:03,901
It must say password,

112
00:04:03,901 --> 00:04:04,150
set.

113
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:08,988
Five: write notes dot text, three lines: where, why, and override.

114
00:04:11,038 --> 00:04:15,241
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen if you need to write it down.

115
00:04:15,791 --> 00:04:17,490
The lab lives on git hub,

116
00:04:17,490 --> 00:04:18,645
at it dash waves,

117
00:04:18,645 --> 00:04:20,208
slash dev ops dash A I,

118
00:04:20,208 --> 00:04:21,703
in the folder academy,

119
00:04:21,703 --> 00:04:22,383
slash lab.

120
00:04:22,933 --> 00:04:27,925
Two files: lab ninety-eight dot S H, and shortcuts ninety-eight dot S H.

121
00:04:28,475 --> 00:04:29,346
Install it,

122
00:04:29,346 --> 00:04:32,911
in your Ubuntu virtual machine: sudo install,

123
00:04:32,911 --> 00:04:34,733
dash m seven five five,

124
00:04:34,733 --> 00:04:36,713
lab ninety-eight dot S H,

125
00:04:36,713 --> 00:04:37,901
into slash usr,

126
00:04:37,901 --> 00:04:38,852
slash local,

127
00:04:38,852 --> 00:04:39,803
slash S bin.

128
00:04:40,353 --> 00:04:44,545
Load the short name with: source shortcuts ninety-eight dot S H.

129
00:04:44,545 --> 00:04:46,249
Then you can type: lab up,

130
00:04:46,249 --> 00:04:46,904
lab check,

131
00:04:46,904 --> 00:04:47,755
and lab down.

132
00:04:48,305 --> 00:04:49,472
You need a J D K,

133
00:04:49,472 --> 00:04:50,982
curl and python three,

134
00:04:50,982 --> 00:04:52,972
about one gigabyte of memory,

135
00:04:52,972 --> 00:04:54,825
and an internet connection.

136
00:04:54,825 --> 00:04:57,159
The first lab up downloads Gradle.

137
00:04:57,709 --> 00:05:01,997
Lab down removes everything. Only run it in your own virtual machine.

138
00:05:04,047 --> 00:05:06,116
Pass or fail. You need all six.

139
00:05:06,666 --> 00:05:08,480
Five pass lines in lab check.

140
00:05:09,030 --> 00:05:10,907
The password text is in no file.

141
00:05:11,457 --> 00:05:15,190
The greeting is in the file, and the override works from the command line.

142
00:05:15,740 --> 00:05:19,303
The secret came from the environment, and show config says set.

143
00:05:19,853 --> 00:05:23,992
Notes dot text answers where, why, and override, in your own words.

144
00:05:24,542 --> 00:05:26,398
Lab down leaves nothing behind.

145
00:05:26,948 --> 00:05:28,249
To pass, all six.

146
00:05:30,299 --> 00:05:33,136
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

147
00:05:33,686 --> 00:05:35,777
One: lab up, and read the task file.

148
00:05:36,327 --> 00:05:38,396
Two: take the password out of the file.

149
00:05:38,946 --> 00:05:41,400
Three: add the greeting, and override it once.

150
00:05:41,950 --> 00:05:44,296
Four: pass the secret through the environment.

151
00:05:44,846 --> 00:05:47,257
Five: write the notes, and run lab check.

152
00:05:47,807 --> 00:05:50,388
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

153
00:05:50,938 --> 00:05:52,773
Pause the video, and begin now.

154
00:06:08,323 --> 00:06:09,198
Quick check.

155
00:06:09,748 --> 00:06:12,372
Where do settings go, and where do secrets go?

156
00:06:12,922 --> 00:06:15,375
Which flag overrides a property for one run?

157
00:06:15,925 --> 00:06:19,338
How does an environment variable become a Gradle property?

158
00:06:19,888 --> 00:06:22,790
Why does show config print set, and not the value?

159
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:29,377
Objective covered: M C eleven, objective four, Gradle environment settings and secrets.

160
00:06:29,927 --> 00:06:31,996
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

161
00:06:42,546 --> 00:06:45,490
Next: the build cache, and reproducible builds.

162
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:49,368
